22
00:01:11,940 --> 00:01:14,450
First off, it is
important to precisely

23
00:01:14,450 --> 00:01:16,730
know the definition
of myocarditis.

24
00:01:16,730 --> 00:01:20,070
The definition is
histopathologic in nature

25
00:01:20,070 --> 00:01:22,410
and is described by
the Dallas criteria.

26
00:01:22,570 --> 00:01:25,490
This criteria is the
presence of an inflammatory

27
00:01:25,490 --> 00:01:28,970
infiltrate of the myocardium
with necrosis and or

28
00:01:28,970 --> 00:01:33,090
degeneration of adjacent
myocytes, not typical of ischemic

29
00:01:33,090 --> 00:01:35,990
damage associated with
coronary artery disease.

30
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:39,090
After a heart attack,
there are dead myocardial

31
00:01:39,090 --> 00:01:41,370
cells. The healing
process and scar formation

32
00:01:41,370 --> 00:01:43,890
involve an influx of
immune cells. Although

33
00:01:43,890 --> 00:01:45,890
there is inflammation
and myocyte necrosis,

34
00:01:45,890 --> 00:01:48,120
in this instance, it
is not myocarditis.

35
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:51,530
The clinical manifestations
of myocarditis

36
00:01:51,530 --> 00:01:53,990
range greatly from
virtually asymptomatic and

37
00:01:53,990 --> 00:01:56,330
self-limited to
fulminant, meaning sudden

38
00:01:56,330 --> 00:01:59,410
escalation of symptoms
with severe heart failure.

39
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:02,170
About half of the
time, an etiologic

40
00:02:02,170 --> 00:02:04,750
agent is never
identified. However,

41
00:02:04,750 --> 00:02:07,170
when there is, it
is usually a virus.

42
00:02:07,290 --> 00:02:10,090
Other significant
causes are bacteria,

43
00:02:10,090 --> 00:02:13,690
fungi, parasites,
cardiotoxins, drugs,

44
00:02:13,690 --> 00:02:16,130
and systemic
autoimmune disorders.

45
00:02:18,770 --> 00:02:22,330
Here are histological
pictures of myocarditis.

46
00:02:22,330 --> 00:02:24,830
Notice the inflammatory
infiltrate of

47
00:02:24,830 --> 00:02:27,070
immune cells within
the myocardium.

48
00:02:27,070 --> 00:02:29,830
With the left picture, the
white arrow is pointing

49
00:02:29,830 --> 00:02:32,070
to a lymphocyte, and the
black arrow is pointing

50
00:02:32,070 --> 00:02:35,670
to myocyte necrosis. The
picture on the right shows

51
00:02:35,670 --> 00:02:39,000
a more zoomed-out
histopathology of myocarditis.

52
00:02:42,270 --> 00:02:45,510
Just some quick
epidemiology of myocarditis.

53
00:02:45,510 --> 00:02:49,690
It has a prevalence of
10.2 to 105.6 per 100

54
00:02:49,690 --> 00:02:52,670
,000. The wide range for
this prevalence is due

55
00:02:52,670 --> 00:02:54,830
to the uncertainty
surrounding true prevalence

56
00:02:54,830 --> 00:02:57,450
and potential underdiagnosis
of the disease.

57
00:02:58,210 --> 00:03:00,330
Myocarditis is most
dangerous within the

58
00:03:00,330 --> 00:03:02,510
first year of life, as
the disease presentation

59
00:03:02,510 --> 00:03:04,890
is more likely to be
fulminant in nature.

60
00:03:05,390 --> 00:03:08,250
There is thought to be
a protective effect of

61
00:03:08,250 --> 00:03:10,830
natural hormonal influences
on immune responses

62
00:03:10,830 --> 00:03:13,310
in women when compared
to men when it comes

63
00:03:13,310 --> 00:03:15,290
to myocarditis, which
is correlated to the

64
00:03:15,290 --> 00:03:18,290
increased death rates
in males after age 15.

65
00:03:18,550 --> 00:03:21,250
The diagnosis of
myocarditis can be very

66
00:03:21,250 --> 00:03:23,810
difficult, especially in
areas that lack proper

67
00:03:23,810 --> 00:03:26,410
diagnostic tools.
and without the gold

68
00:03:26,410 --> 00:03:29,030
standard endomyocardial
biopsy, which is another

69
00:03:29,030 --> 00:03:31,270
reason for the wide
range and prevalence.

70
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:37,450
Clinically, there
is a wide range of

71
00:03:37,450 --> 00:03:39,570
symptoms that
accompany myocarditis.

72
00:03:39,570 --> 00:03:42,590
A patient may be completely
asymptomatic and not even

73
00:03:42,590 --> 00:03:45,430
know that they have
inflammation of the heart. On

74
00:03:45,430 --> 00:03:47,550
the opposite side of the
spectrum, they may develop

75
00:03:47,550 --> 00:03:50,870
dilated cardiomyopathy or
arrhythmias that can cause

76
00:03:50,870 --> 00:03:53,910
sudden death, which
describes more of a fulminant

77
00:03:53,910 --> 00:03:57,410
clinical course. The symptoms
that lie between these

78
00:03:57,410 --> 00:04:01,790
two extremes include fatigue,
dyspnea, palpitations,

79
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:04,370
precordial
discomfort, and fever.

80
00:04:04,370 --> 00:04:07,630
The trickiness of diagnosis
increases even more

81
00:04:07,630 --> 00:04:10,890
when myocarditis symptoms
mimic acute MI symptoms.

82
00:04:11,350 --> 00:04:14,330
Patients can present
with chest pain, EKG

83
00:04:14,330 --> 00:04:17,490
abnormalities, and elevated
cardiac biomarkers.

84
00:04:20,510 --> 00:04:24,370
diagnosis of myocarditis
requires clues from both the

85
00:04:24,370 --> 00:04:27,710
history and physical and
diagnostic tests although

86
00:04:27,710 --> 00:04:31,910
not regularly used an
endomyocardial biopsy or EMB is

87
00:04:31,910 --> 00:04:35,390
the gold standard it is
done if other non-invasive

88
00:04:35,390 --> 00:04:38,630
modalities cannot reach a
diagnosis and if the results

89
00:04:38,630 --> 00:04:41,910
of the EMB significantly
impact patient management.

90
00:04:42,030 --> 00:04:46,130
It is performed by inserting
a bioptome into the

91
00:04:46,130 --> 00:04:48,550
venous system and into
the right ventricle, or a

92
00:04:48,550 --> 00:04:51,380
sample is taken and can be
viewed for histopathology.

93
00:04:52,430 --> 00:04:54,970
EKG, CRP, troponin,

94
00:04:55,130 --> 00:04:57,490
chest radiograph, and
echocardiogram are

95
00:04:57,490 --> 00:05:00,230
always needed when
myocarditis is suspected.

96
00:05:00,490 --> 00:05:03,170
One of the methods for
determining if a patient

97
00:05:03,170 --> 00:05:05,450
is presenting with acute
coronary syndrome or

98
00:05:05,450 --> 00:05:09,830
myocarditis is to take the
ratio of CRP to troponin.

99
00:05:10,050 --> 00:05:13,670
Those with acute coronary
syndrome will have much

100
00:05:13,670 --> 00:05:17,450
lower CRP to troponin ratio,
meaning the CRP levels are

101
00:05:17,450 --> 00:05:20,510
lower and troponins are higher
compared to myocarditis,

102
00:05:20,510 --> 00:05:23,890
which has higher CRP
levels and lower troponins.

103
00:05:24,350 --> 00:05:27,090
If acute coronary
syndrome cannot be ruled

104
00:05:27,090 --> 00:05:30,130
out, then you may need
coronary angiography.

105
00:05:30,890 --> 00:05:33,450
Additionally, a definitive
diagnosis cannot

106
00:05:33,450 --> 00:05:36,470
be made without an
EMB that meets Dallas

107
00:05:36,470 --> 00:05:39,530
criteria, as well as an
EMB sample that indicates

108
00:05:39,530 --> 00:05:42,630
myocarditis with
immunohistochemical stains.

109
00:05:43,190 --> 00:05:46,070
If myocarditis is
likely based on history

110
00:05:46,070 --> 00:05:48,730
and physical and non
-invasive tests, then it's

111
00:05:48,730 --> 00:05:51,550
termed clinically
suspected myocarditis.

112
00:05:54,270 --> 00:05:57,310
Myocarditis can be
classified into four distinct

113
00:05:57,310 --> 00:06:00,190
clinical presentations with
their own unique courses.

114
00:06:00,470 --> 00:06:03,230
The two acute forms
are on this slide,

115
00:06:03,350 --> 00:06:05,210
acute and fulminant.

116
00:06:05,210 --> 00:06:07,430
Acute myocarditis is usually

117
00:06:07,430 --> 00:06:09,050
caused by a viral infection.

118
00:06:09,090 --> 00:06:11,730
We will go into exactly
what viruses tend

119
00:06:11,730 --> 00:06:14,270
to cause myocarditis
later in this lecture.

120
00:06:14,450 --> 00:06:17,570
It occurs two to four
weeks after exposure.

121
00:06:17,630 --> 00:06:20,450
This clinical manifestation
has the highest

122
00:06:20,450 --> 00:06:22,770
risk of dilated
cardiomyopathy in the

123
00:06:22,770 --> 00:06:25,850
future among acute
versions of myocarditis.

124
00:06:26,250 --> 00:06:29,130
Physical exam of acute
myocarditis may show

125
00:06:29,130 --> 00:06:33,050
a third heart sound,
such as S3 or S4, which

126
00:06:33,050 --> 00:06:35,150
are indicative of
pathology of the heart.

127
00:06:35,570 --> 00:06:38,870
Mitral or tricuspid
insufficiency murmurs can be

128
00:06:38,870 --> 00:06:41,350
heard from dilation of the
heart and separation of

129
00:06:41,350 --> 00:06:44,610
the valve leaflets if dilated
cardiomyopathy occurs.

130
00:06:44,890 --> 00:06:48,010
A pericardial friction
rub may be heard if

131
00:06:48,010 --> 00:06:50,660
there is also
superimposed pericarditis.

132
00:06:50,870 --> 00:06:52,730
Heart failure findings, such

133
00:06:52,730 --> 00:06:54,930
as fluid overload, may result.

134
00:06:55,690 --> 00:06:58,770
Fulminant myocarditis has
a much more severe acute

135
00:06:58,770 --> 00:07:02,030
presentation and much
quicker onset of symptoms.

136
00:07:02,290 --> 00:07:04,430
It usually results
within two weeks

137
00:07:04,430 --> 00:07:06,650
of exposure to the
etiologic agent.

138
00:07:06,870 --> 00:07:09,190
It is accompanied by
severe dysfunction of

139
00:07:09,190 --> 00:07:11,770
the left ventricle,
leading to heart failure.

140
00:07:12,070 --> 00:07:14,230
Histology will show
many areas of active

141
00:07:14,230 --> 00:07:17,170
inflammation and necrosis
of cardiomyocytes.

142
00:07:17,450 --> 00:07:20,270
Patients either die from
the severity of the heart

143
00:07:20,270 --> 00:07:23,910
dysfunction or surprisingly
fully recover, having a

144
00:07:23,910 --> 00:07:27,290
better long-term prognosis
than acute myocarditis.

145
00:07:30,250 --> 00:07:32,590
These are the two
versions of chronic

146
00:07:32,590 --> 00:07:35,150
myocarditis that you
are responsible for.

147
00:07:35,190 --> 00:07:37,750
Chronic active myocarditis has

148
00:07:37,750 --> 00:07:39,810
symptoms present
after two weeks.

149
00:07:39,900 --> 00:07:42,640
There is a long-term
active inflammatory

150
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:44,950
infiltrate within the
myocardium that ends up

151
00:07:44,950 --> 00:07:47,990
activating fibroblasts,
leading to fibrosis.

152
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:50,830
As a result of this,
the heart is at risk of

153
00:07:50,830 --> 00:07:53,730
developing restrictive
cardiomyopathy, as

154
00:07:53,730 --> 00:07:55,990
opposed to the dilated
cardiomyopathy that

155
00:07:55,990 --> 00:07:58,750
you see with acute and
fulminant myocarditis.

156
00:07:59,150 --> 00:08:01,730
The top right picture
shows the inflammatory

157
00:08:01,730 --> 00:08:04,410
infiltrate and fibrosis
within the myocardium.

158
00:08:04,490 --> 00:08:06,930
This takes time,
however, developing in

159
00:08:06,930 --> 00:08:08,950
two to four years
after presentation.

160
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:12,370
Chronic persistent, as
the name suggests, is

161
00:08:12,370 --> 00:08:14,610
persistent infiltrate
of immune cells and

162
00:08:14,610 --> 00:08:17,670
persistent symptoms of
myocarditis. However,

163
00:08:17,670 --> 00:08:20,250
there is no ventricular
dysfunction present.

164
00:08:23,810 --> 00:08:26,270
Now that we have
discussed how a person

165
00:08:26,270 --> 00:08:28,250
with myocarditis
presents, we will go

166
00:08:28,250 --> 00:08:30,330
into what agents
leads the condition.

167
00:08:30,350 --> 00:08:33,890
These are viral,
bacterial, fungal,

168
00:08:33,890 --> 00:08:36,850
parasitic, and immune
-mediated causes.

169
00:08:39,610 --> 00:08:42,590
The most common
cause of myocarditis,

170
00:08:42,590 --> 00:08:45,410
specifically acute
myocarditis, when an

171
00:08:45,410 --> 00:08:47,850
etiology is identified,
are viruses.

172
00:08:48,030 --> 00:08:51,210
The viruses most
associated with myocarditis

173
00:08:51,210 --> 00:08:54,770
are enteroviruses,
specifically Coxsackie B.

174
00:08:54,780 --> 00:08:58,200
This virus is also
associated with pleurodynia,

175
00:08:58,200 --> 00:09:01,850
or severe spastic pain
caused by myositis of

176
00:09:01,850 --> 00:09:05,090
the abdomen or chest,
as well as GI distress,

177
00:09:05,210 --> 00:09:06,070
fever,

178
00:09:06,190 --> 00:09:10,230
headache, sore throat,
and aseptic meningitis.

179
00:09:10,450 --> 00:09:13,930
Recently, myocarditis
caused by parvovirus

180
00:09:13,930 --> 00:09:18,050
B19 and HHV-6 have
become more common.

181
00:09:18,350 --> 00:09:22,690
CMV, HIV, and influenza
can also cause

182
00:09:22,690 --> 00:09:24,890
myocarditis, although
less commonly.

183
00:09:25,330 --> 00:09:28,190
Identification of the
virus uses serologic

184
00:09:28,190 --> 00:09:30,250
studies, which are
much less invasive

185
00:09:30,250 --> 00:09:32,690
than the rarely used
viral nucleic acid

186
00:09:32,690 --> 00:09:35,830
sequencing obtained from
myocardial biopsies.

187
00:09:36,390 --> 00:09:39,570
Viruses damage the
heart via two methods,

188
00:09:39,570 --> 00:09:42,430
direct damage to the
cardiomyocytes by

189
00:09:42,430 --> 00:09:44,990
the virus or secondary
damage caused by the

190
00:09:44,990 --> 00:09:47,030
immune cells that
respond to the virus.

191
00:09:47,030 --> 00:09:49,590
The picture on the right
shows the Coxsackie

192
00:09:49,590 --> 00:09:52,450
B virus obtained from
an electron microscope.

193
00:09:55,330 --> 00:09:58,310
Bacteria may also
cause myocarditis.

194
00:09:58,550 --> 00:10:01,310
Chlamydia, Rickettsia,
and Neisseria are all

195
00:10:01,310 --> 00:10:03,970
potential etiologic
agents. However, the most

196
00:10:03,970 --> 00:10:07,050
important ones to know for
board exams are Borrelia

197
00:10:07,050 --> 00:10:10,270
burgdorferi, which
causes Lyme disease, and

198
00:10:10,270 --> 00:10:13,970
Crinobacterium diphtheria,
which causes diphtheria.

199
00:10:14,450 --> 00:10:16,850
Borrelia burgdorferi
is a spirochete

200
00:10:16,850 --> 00:10:18,510
spread by the exotis tick.

201
00:10:18,670 --> 00:10:21,650
The bacteria infiltrate
the heart and can cause an

202
00:10:21,650 --> 00:10:25,230
inflammatory response termed
Lyme carditis. The most

203
00:10:25,230 --> 00:10:28,310
classic presentation of this
is a rapidly changing AV

204
00:10:28,310 --> 00:10:32,270
block, meaning the EKG may
first show first degree,

205
00:10:32,270 --> 00:10:34,930
then second degree, and
progress to complete heart

206
00:10:34,930 --> 00:10:38,130
block, then return back to
first degree within minutes.

207
00:10:38,810 --> 00:10:41,590
Diphtheria is commonly
associated with pseudomembrane

208
00:10:41,590 --> 00:10:44,390
and can form on the tonsils
and throat by destroying

209
00:10:44,390 --> 00:10:47,250
healthy tissue as well as
causing a swollen neck.

210
00:10:47,820 --> 00:10:50,730
Diphtheria produces a
toxin that can leak into

211
00:10:50,730 --> 00:10:53,850
the lymphatic and
hematologic systems and can

212
00:10:53,850 --> 00:10:56,240
cause damage to the heart,
leading to myocarditis.

213
00:10:57,050 --> 00:10:59,450
Diphtheria toxin
damages tissues by

214
00:10:59,450 --> 00:11:02,910
inhibiting elongation
factor 2, or EF2,

215
00:11:02,910 --> 00:11:05,450
which is important
for protein synthesis.

216
00:11:08,890 --> 00:11:10,630
Next is fungi.

217
00:11:10,630 --> 00:11:13,610
This etiology is very
rare, but most commonly

218
00:11:13,610 --> 00:11:16,870
seen in immunocompromised
individuals. So the

219
00:11:16,870 --> 00:11:19,670
risk of fungal myocarditis
is highest in those

220
00:11:19,670 --> 00:11:22,630
with long-term, broad
-spectrum antibiotic usage,

221
00:11:22,850 --> 00:11:25,250
corticosteroid usage, invasive

222
00:11:25,250 --> 00:11:28,490
procedures, and those
with HIV infection.

223
00:11:28,670 --> 00:11:31,730
Definitive diagnosis is
very difficult based on

224
00:11:31,730 --> 00:11:34,430
non-invasive diagnostic
tests since the clinical

225
00:11:34,430 --> 00:11:37,230
signs are absent and blood
tests are often negative.

226
00:11:37,430 --> 00:11:39,710
The most common
fungal causes are

227
00:11:39,710 --> 00:11:43,130
invasive Candida or
Aspergillus species.

228
00:11:43,370 --> 00:11:46,730
On EMB, you may see the
hyphae, as in the case of

229
00:11:46,730 --> 00:11:49,850
aspergillus, or pseudohyphae,
as in the case of candida.

230
00:11:50,010 --> 00:11:52,710
The picture in the
slide shows invasive

231
00:11:52,710 --> 00:11:55,810
aspergillus, which has
spread to the heart, causing

232
00:11:55,810 --> 00:11:58,970
myocarditis. You can
see the septate hyphae.

233
00:12:01,550 --> 00:12:04,350
Here are the most common
parasitic causes of

234
00:12:04,350 --> 00:12:08,110
myocarditis. The most heavily
tested cause of parasitic

235
00:12:08,110 --> 00:12:11,290
myocarditis is Chagas
disease. This is the most

236
00:12:11,290 --> 00:12:13,570
common in Latin America
due to the presence of

237
00:12:13,570 --> 00:12:16,190
the reduvid bug, also known
as the kissing bug, that

238
00:12:16,190 --> 00:12:19,210
spreads the parasite
called trypanosoma cruzi.

239
00:12:19,510 --> 00:12:21,250
They get their
name because they

240
00:12:21,250 --> 00:12:22,870
tend to bite people's faces.

241
00:12:23,170 --> 00:12:25,830
Their urine and feces
carries the parasite,

242
00:12:25,830 --> 00:12:28,530
which can enter the bite
site, causing infection.

243
00:12:29,250 --> 00:12:31,850
Chagas disease usually
comes in phases, with

244
00:12:31,850 --> 00:12:33,970
the acute phase
accompanied usually with

245
00:12:33,970 --> 00:12:36,450
minor symptoms, but can
occasionally be severe

246
00:12:36,450 --> 00:12:40,190
and show signs of CNS
involvement and death.

247
00:12:40,670 --> 00:12:43,510
A characteristic nodule
called the chagoma at

248
00:12:43,510 --> 00:12:45,710
the site of infection
may occur, and if it is

249
00:12:45,710 --> 00:12:48,310
on the eyelid, this is
known as Romagna's sign.

250
00:12:48,410 --> 00:12:50,790
After the acute
phase, which lasts 8

251
00:12:50,790 --> 00:12:53,190
to 12 weeks, the
indeterminate phase

252
00:12:53,190 --> 00:12:55,190
occurs where there
are no symptoms.

253
00:12:55,370 --> 00:12:58,390
The chronic phase
occurs 10 to 20 years

254
00:12:58,390 --> 00:13:00,890
after initial infection.
From the years of

255
00:13:00,890 --> 00:13:03,330
parasite proliferation
in the tissues, patients

256
00:13:03,330 --> 00:13:05,830
develop the characteristic
cardiomegaly,

257
00:13:06,170 --> 00:13:08,430
megaesophagus, and megacolon.

258
00:13:08,530 --> 00:13:11,750
On biopsy, you can see
pseudocyst dilations

259
00:13:11,750 --> 00:13:15,390
within the fibers in
the amastigote form.

260
00:13:15,390 --> 00:13:18,330
The parasite becomes
flagellated when they burst out

261
00:13:18,330 --> 00:13:21,190
of infected cells, which
can be seen on the left.

262
00:13:22,090 --> 00:13:24,430
Toxoplasma gondii
and trichinella

263
00:13:24,430 --> 00:13:26,270
may also lead to myocarditis.

264
00:13:29,490 --> 00:13:32,270
Myocarditis may also
be immune-mediated.

265
00:13:32,650 --> 00:13:35,390
Myocarditis can occur
following a viral infection

266
00:13:35,390 --> 00:13:38,390
with viruses discussed
before, such as Coxsackie

267
00:13:38,390 --> 00:13:44,190
B and other enteroviruses,
parvovirus B19, HHV6.

268
00:13:44,230 --> 00:13:47,270
In this version, the
inflammatory infiltrate is

269
00:13:47,270 --> 00:13:50,370
largely lymphocytic in
nature, which ends up damaging

270
00:13:50,370 --> 00:13:53,850
the heart tissue. If the
inflammatory infiltrate on

271
00:13:53,850 --> 00:13:57,570
EMB has a high proportion
of eosinophils, you would

272
00:13:57,570 --> 00:13:59,530
suspect that the myocarditis
was triggered by a

273
00:13:59,530 --> 00:14:03,210
hypersensitivity response,
most likely from medications.

274
00:14:03,830 --> 00:14:06,130
Ampicillin and
thiazide diuretics are

275
00:14:06,130 --> 00:14:08,190
notable examples of
potential causes.

276
00:14:08,830 --> 00:14:11,330
A very serious immune-mediated

277
00:14:11,330 --> 00:14:14,470
myocarditis that usually
takes on a fulminant

278
00:14:14,470 --> 00:14:16,430
course is giant
cell myocarditis.

279
00:14:16,710 --> 00:14:19,290
There is no known direct
cause of this type, so

280
00:14:19,290 --> 00:14:22,110
it is idiopathic, but
there is an increased risk

281
00:14:22,110 --> 00:14:24,550
among those with concurrent
autoimmune diseases.

282
00:14:25,190 --> 00:14:28,350
EMB will show multinucleated
giant cells as seen in

283
00:14:28,350 --> 00:14:31,830
the picture with a mix of
lymphocytes, eosinophils,

284
00:14:31,990 --> 00:14:36,230
plasma cells, and macrophages.
To give an idea of

285
00:14:36,230 --> 00:14:39,250
severity of this disease,
according to one study, the

286
00:14:39,250 --> 00:14:43,310
rate of death or cardiac
transplant was 89%, and the

287
00:14:43,310 --> 00:14:46,870
median survival from onset
of symptoms was 5.5 months.

288
00:14:50,310 --> 00:14:52,930
Continuing our discussion
on immune causes,

289
00:14:52,930 --> 00:14:54,890
the immune system of
the host can attack a

290
00:14:54,890 --> 00:14:57,190
donor heart, causing
transplant rejection.

291
00:14:57,270 --> 00:15:00,660
An EMB will show
inflammatory infiltrate and

292
00:15:00,660 --> 00:15:04,020
cardiomyocyte cell death, so
this would be myocarditis.

293
00:15:04,610 --> 00:15:08,450
Additionally, rheumatic fever
caused after a streptococcal

294
00:15:08,450 --> 00:15:11,570
infection, specifically
group A strep, may lead

295
00:15:11,570 --> 00:15:14,990
to myocarditis. This occurs
due to a highly antigenic

296
00:15:14,990 --> 00:15:18,050
protein released by the
bacteria called M protein,

297
00:15:18,050 --> 00:15:22,990
an NABG, also known as N
-acetyl-beta-D-glucosamine.

298
00:15:23,490 --> 00:15:26,290
Antibodies against
protein M can cross-react

299
00:15:26,290 --> 00:15:28,500
with the myosin within
the cardiomyocytes,

300
00:15:28,500 --> 00:15:31,830
leading to damage in
antibodies against NABG

301
00:15:31,830 --> 00:15:34,350
likely to play a role
in valvular injury.

302
00:15:34,350 --> 00:15:37,890
The histopathology of
heart tissue and rheumatic

303
00:15:37,890 --> 00:15:41,570
fever will show Ashkoff
bodies, which are granulomas,

304
00:15:41,570 --> 00:15:45,330
as well as Anishkoff cells,
also known as caterpillar

305
00:15:45,330 --> 00:15:48,510
cells, which are macrophages
with ovoid nucleus.

306
00:15:48,510 --> 00:15:50,510
The elongated nucleus somewhat

307
00:15:50,510 --> 00:15:52,110
resembles a caterpillar.

308
00:15:52,330 --> 00:15:55,490
An Ashkoff body and
Anishkoff cell can

309
00:15:55,490 --> 00:15:57,410
be seen in the
picture on the right.

310
00:15:57,850 --> 00:16:01,090
Myocarditis may also be seen
in inflammatory systemic

311
00:16:01,090 --> 00:16:04,890
disorders. In all cases,
inflammatory cells

312
00:16:04,890 --> 00:16:08,210
may infiltrate the myocardium,
causing myocarditis.

313
00:16:11,150 --> 00:16:13,910
The final cause
of myocarditis we

314
00:16:13,910 --> 00:16:15,950
will discuss is
direct cardiotoxins.

315
00:16:16,250 --> 00:16:18,230
They induce myocarditis through

316
00:16:18,230 --> 00:16:20,150
mechanisms that are
not well elucidated.

317
00:16:20,370 --> 00:16:23,450
You'll see this with
antineoplastic agents and

318
00:16:23,450 --> 00:16:26,570
treatments like anthracyclines
and cyclophosphamide,

319
00:16:26,570 --> 00:16:30,510
as well as radiation. In
addition, illicit drugs

320
00:16:30,510 --> 00:16:33,950
like cocaine, heavy alcohol
use, certain metals like

321
00:16:33,950 --> 00:16:36,390
copper, lead, and iron
can lead to myocarditis.

322
00:16:37,040 --> 00:16:40,070
To give some visuals, on the
top right is cocaine, and

323
00:16:40,070 --> 00:16:43,570
below is arsenic, and below
that is doxorubicin, and

324
00:16:43,570 --> 00:16:46,650
anthracycline, which has a
characteristic red color.

325
00:16:49,070 --> 00:16:51,850
The next section of this
lecture is pericardial

326
00:16:51,850 --> 00:16:54,470
disease. This has to do
with the pericardium,

327
00:16:54,470 --> 00:16:56,390
which is the sac
surrounding the heart that

328
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:58,970
provides mechanical
protection and lubrication

329
00:16:58,970 --> 00:17:01,110
between the heart and the
surrounding structures.

330
00:17:01,320 --> 00:17:03,490
Between the heart and
the pericardium is the

331
00:17:03,490 --> 00:17:05,670
pericardial space,
or a small amount of

332
00:17:05,670 --> 00:17:08,470
serous fluid, which
allows that lubrication.

333
00:17:08,490 --> 00:17:11,410
The disease of the pericardium
and the pericardial

334
00:17:11,410 --> 00:17:13,970
space occur from either
direct disease or

335
00:17:13,970 --> 00:17:17,790
indirectly through systemic
diseases. It manifests

336
00:17:17,790 --> 00:17:20,410
from fluid buildup in
the pericardial space,

337
00:17:20,410 --> 00:17:22,750
which is also known as
pericardial effusion,

338
00:17:22,770 --> 00:17:26,030
inflammation of the pericardium,
termed pericarditis,

339
00:17:26,290 --> 00:17:29,870
and or fibrous constriction,
which occurs when

340
00:17:29,870 --> 00:17:32,590
excess fibrin deposition
happens, and the

341
00:17:32,590 --> 00:17:35,690
pericardium becomes
thickened and non-compliant.

342
00:17:39,450 --> 00:17:43,030
normally the pericardial
space contains around 50

343
00:17:43,030 --> 00:17:46,230
milliliters of serous fluid
if you were to see the fluid

344
00:17:46,230 --> 00:17:48,090
it would appear like the
fluid in the picture at

345
00:17:48,090 --> 00:17:51,270
the top right this yellowish
color is termed straw

346
00:17:51,270 --> 00:17:54,930
colored when fluids such as
serious fluid or other foods

347
00:17:54,930 --> 00:17:58,110
like blood pus or lymphatic
fluid build up in the

348
00:17:58,110 --> 00:18:01,950
pericardial space it is
called pericardial effusion

349
00:18:05,430 --> 00:18:08,430
the pericardium has the
ability to adapt to changes

350
00:18:08,430 --> 00:18:11,070
in the volume of pericardial
fluid but only if

351
00:18:11,070 --> 00:18:14,210
it is a slow buildup it
remodels and gets bigger

352
00:18:14,210 --> 00:18:17,850
allowing for cardiac function
to go unaffected some

353
00:18:17,850 --> 00:18:19,750
patients may not even
know that they have a

354
00:18:19,750 --> 00:18:22,910
pericardial effusion if they
have less than 500 milliliters

355
00:18:22,970 --> 00:18:26,670
and it is chronic x-ray
will show an enlarged

356
00:18:26,670 --> 00:18:28,850
heart shadow and is
known as a water bottle

357
00:18:28,850 --> 00:18:32,390
configuration, as you can
see in the top right picture.

358
00:18:32,910 --> 00:18:35,210
Pericardial effusions
are very dangerous as

359
00:18:35,210 --> 00:18:37,510
the fluid in the pericardial
space accumulates

360
00:18:37,510 --> 00:18:39,530
very rapidly to the
point where the fluid

361
00:18:39,530 --> 00:18:42,250
compresses the heart so
much that it cannot fill

362
00:18:42,250 --> 00:18:45,690
properly. This is termed
cardiac tamponade.

363
00:18:45,910 --> 00:18:49,210
A commonly tested version
of this is hemopericardium

364
00:18:49,210 --> 00:18:51,990
or accumulation of blood in
the space from the rupture

365
00:18:51,990 --> 00:18:55,770
of the heart after an MI or
a type A aortic dissection

366
00:18:55,770 --> 00:18:59,730
if it includes the
pericardium only 200 to 300

367
00:18:59,730 --> 00:19:02,480
milliliters is required for
this presentation since the

368
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:05,450
pericardium does not have any
time to adapt to the increased

369
00:19:05,450 --> 00:19:12,250
fluid these are the forms
of acute pericarditis

370
00:19:12,250 --> 00:19:14,830
you are responsible for
knowing they are caused by

371
00:19:14,830 --> 00:19:17,480
different etiologies and
present differently both

372
00:19:17,480 --> 00:19:21,790
macroscopically and on histology
the terms before the word

373
00:19:21,790 --> 00:19:24,470
pericarditis describe what
you will see grossly if you

374
00:19:24,470 --> 00:19:27,150
were to look at the pericardium
and pericardial space.

375
00:19:27,390 --> 00:19:29,510
There are also chronic forms of

376
00:19:29,510 --> 00:19:31,710
pericarditis, which
we will go into later.

377
00:19:34,970 --> 00:19:38,070
First off is serous
pericarditis. This one

378
00:19:38,070 --> 00:19:40,010
tends to occur due
to mainly systemic

379
00:19:40,010 --> 00:19:42,830
inflammatory diseases
and not from infection.

380
00:19:43,010 --> 00:19:45,610
There's a collection
of excess serous fluid

381
00:19:45,610 --> 00:19:48,090
in the pericardial
space, which can be seen

382
00:19:48,090 --> 00:19:49,870
in the picture on the
top right of a heart

383
00:19:49,870 --> 00:19:52,090
from a patient with
rheumatoid arthritis.

384
00:19:52,670 --> 00:19:54,670
Besides rheumatoid
arthritis, you can

385
00:19:54,670 --> 00:19:56,770
see serous pericarditis
and rheumatic

386
00:19:56,770 --> 00:20:00,070
fever, systemic
lupus erythematosus,

387
00:20:00,270 --> 00:20:02,230
scleroderma, tumors,

388
00:20:02,450 --> 00:20:04,210
and uremia, among others.

389
00:20:04,500 --> 00:20:07,490
There may be an infectious
process going on, but not

390
00:20:07,490 --> 00:20:10,610
directly in the pericardial
space or pericardium.

391
00:20:10,610 --> 00:20:13,690
By extension, there is
irritation, which can cause

392
00:20:13,690 --> 00:20:16,950
mild inflammatory infiltrate
and an increase in serious

393
00:20:16,950 --> 00:20:20,530
fluid accumulation. If
infection is involved, be

394
00:20:20,530 --> 00:20:23,230
careful about evolving into
either serofibrinous or

395
00:20:23,230 --> 00:20:26,830
suppurative pericarditis,
which we will soon discuss.

396
00:20:27,350 --> 00:20:30,910
Viruses can also cause serous
pericarditis, and commonly

397
00:20:30,910 --> 00:20:33,390
someone will have a viral
infection of the upper

398
00:20:33,390 --> 00:20:37,070
airway or the lungs. It is
most likely not a direct

399
00:20:37,070 --> 00:20:39,950
infection of the pericardium,
and direct infections

400
00:20:39,950 --> 00:20:43,110
are rare and are usually
associated with myocarditis.

401
00:20:43,910 --> 00:20:46,550
Tumors lead to serous
pericarditis through

402
00:20:46,550 --> 00:20:49,610
invasion of the
lymphatics. There is a mild

403
00:20:49,610 --> 00:20:52,150
inflammatory infiltrate
involved consisting of

404
00:20:52,150 --> 00:20:54,970
lymphocytes, and pericardial
fluid analysis may

405
00:20:54,970 --> 00:20:58,270
contain neoplastic cells
when cancer is involved.

406
00:21:01,210 --> 00:21:05,510
Next up is serofibrinous
and fibrinous pericarditis.

407
00:21:05,770 --> 00:21:08,490
Serofibrinous involves
both serous effusion

408
00:21:08,490 --> 00:21:11,610
with fibrin deposition,
while fibrinous is mainly

409
00:21:11,610 --> 00:21:14,130
fibrin deposition
covering the pericardium.

410
00:21:14,220 --> 00:21:17,380
How it appears is classically
termed bread-and-butter

411
00:21:17,380 --> 00:21:20,010
pericarditis, since it kind
of looks as if two pieces

412
00:21:20,010 --> 00:21:22,430
of buttered bread were
pressed together then pulled

413
00:21:22,430 --> 00:21:26,090
apart. This is the most common
type of pericarditis and is

414
00:21:26,090 --> 00:21:29,730
associated with acute
myocardial infarction, uremia,

415
00:21:29,870 --> 00:21:31,190
rheumatic fever,

416
00:21:31,330 --> 00:21:34,850
lupus, trauma, and
after cardiac surgery.

417
00:21:35,430 --> 00:21:38,170
Dressler syndrome is a topic
commonly found in questions

418
00:21:38,170 --> 00:21:41,390
and happens usually one to
six weeks after myocardial

419
00:21:41,390 --> 00:21:44,710
infarction or after heart
surgery. It is thought

420
00:21:44,710 --> 00:21:47,590
to happen from release of
antigens from the pericardium

421
00:21:47,590 --> 00:21:50,790
and heart that our immune
system detects as foreign.

422
00:21:50,910 --> 00:21:53,890
The classic sign of
pericarditis is the friction

423
00:21:53,890 --> 00:21:57,530
rub herb with a stethoscope.
The patient may also

424
00:21:57,530 --> 00:21:59,970
assume the tripod position
where they lean forward

425
00:21:59,970 --> 00:22:02,890
supporting their upper
body on the knees or other

426
00:22:02,890 --> 00:22:05,350
surface. This is seen
mostly in respiratory

427
00:22:05,350 --> 00:22:08,490
distress, but in a patient
with chest pain without labor

428
00:22:08,490 --> 00:22:10,950
breathing, this can be
a sign of pericarditis.

429
00:22:14,430 --> 00:22:17,250
When pus is seen
surrounding the heart, this

430
00:22:17,250 --> 00:22:19,570
indicates that an active
infection is present.

431
00:22:19,570 --> 00:22:22,190
This can be direct
infection from trauma or

432
00:22:22,190 --> 00:22:24,050
surgery, or it can
spread from a neighboring

433
00:22:24,050 --> 00:22:26,690
structure, like from a
pneumonia of the lungs,

434
00:22:26,850 --> 00:22:29,590
mediastinal infection,
or abscess of the heart.

435
00:22:30,200 --> 00:22:32,410
Bacteria can also travel
through the blood to the

436
00:22:32,410 --> 00:22:35,770
pericardium, or through the
lymphatics. the picture on

437
00:22:35,770 --> 00:22:37,830
the right demonstrates
purulent fluid and the

438
00:22:37,830 --> 00:22:42,230
pericardial sac with erythematous
changes of the pericardium

439
00:22:44,420 --> 00:22:49,350
here we have hemorrhagic
pericarditis if you were

440
00:22:49,350 --> 00:22:51,610
to open up the pericardium
and look inside you'll

441
00:22:51,610 --> 00:22:55,660
see blood with fibrinous
or suppurative effusion you

442
00:22:55,710 --> 00:22:58,450
will see this with mostly
malignancy and you'll see

443
00:22:58,450 --> 00:23:02,870
neoplastic cells on pericardial
tap bacterial infection

444
00:23:02,870 --> 00:23:06,030
can also cause this most
commonly, tuberculosis.

445
00:23:06,510 --> 00:23:08,970
There's also a chance
at developing this form

446
00:23:08,970 --> 00:23:11,110
if the patient has an
increased tendency to

447
00:23:11,110 --> 00:23:14,140
bleed. This is known
as bleeding diastasis.

448
00:23:14,790 --> 00:23:17,270
Anytime there is surgery
and there is a risk of

449
00:23:17,270 --> 00:23:19,550
damaging the vasculature
in the area, bleeding

450
00:23:19,550 --> 00:23:22,490
and inflammation can
result, and if it is in this

451
00:23:22,490 --> 00:23:25,770
area of the pericardium,
this form can manifest.

452
00:23:25,960 --> 00:23:27,770
The picture on the
right shows the

453
00:23:27,770 --> 00:23:29,350
blood and the
fibrinous adhesions

454
00:23:29,350 --> 00:23:31,460
connecting the heart
to the pericardium.

455
00:23:34,870 --> 00:23:38,790
Here are the two chronic or
healed forms of pericarditis

456
00:23:38,790 --> 00:23:41,150
that we will discuss.
They are adhesive

457
00:23:41,150 --> 00:23:45,370
mediastino-pericarditis and
constrictive pericarditis.

458
00:23:45,510 --> 00:23:48,710
Chronic pericarditis is
associated with fibrosis

459
00:23:48,710 --> 00:23:51,490
of the pericardium, the
level of which varies

460
00:23:51,490 --> 00:23:54,330
from a few unobstructive
fibrous thickenings

461
00:23:54,330 --> 00:23:57,050
called soldier's plaques
to large mesh-like

462
00:23:57,050 --> 00:24:00,330
adhesions that take up the
whole pericardial space.

463
00:24:00,610 --> 00:24:03,050
Since this is chronic,
the heart is still

464
00:24:03,050 --> 00:24:05,110
able to function and
keep the patient alive

465
00:24:05,110 --> 00:24:08,010
despite what is going
on with the pericardium.

466
00:24:08,170 --> 00:24:11,730
This is because the pericardium
has time to remodel.

467
00:24:15,670 --> 00:24:18,590
Adhesive mediastinal
pericarditis is interesting

468
00:24:18,590 --> 00:24:21,470
because it involves adhesions
on the external surface

469
00:24:21,470 --> 00:24:24,490
of the parietal or outside
layer of the pericardium

470
00:24:24,490 --> 00:24:27,610
as opposed to the serosal
layer or inside layer.

471
00:24:27,810 --> 00:24:30,750
These adhesions form
as a result of previous

472
00:24:30,750 --> 00:24:34,110
infectious pericarditis,
previous surgery, or

473
00:24:34,110 --> 00:24:37,050
radiation. It can attach
to structures surrounding

474
00:24:37,050 --> 00:24:38,990
the heart so that
with each beat these

475
00:24:38,990 --> 00:24:42,290
adhesions become taut and
strain cardiac function.

476
00:24:42,430 --> 00:24:45,770
The heart will, as a
result, have systolic

477
00:24:45,770 --> 00:24:49,070
dysfunction, and in some
cases there will be retraction

478
00:24:49,070 --> 00:24:51,530
of the rib cage and
diaphragm during systole

479
00:24:51,530 --> 00:24:53,750
from the heart pulling
on these structures.

480
00:24:54,410 --> 00:24:56,770
Pulsus paradoxus
may happen since

481
00:24:56,770 --> 00:24:58,490
the heart is adherent
to the lungs.

482
00:24:58,910 --> 00:25:01,150
With this strain on
the heart, it forces

483
00:25:01,150 --> 00:25:03,710
it to work harder to
pump. As a result, the

484
00:25:03,710 --> 00:25:06,170
heart hypertrophies
and dilation occurs.

485
00:25:09,830 --> 00:25:13,050
To end our discussion on
pericarditis, the last

486
00:25:13,050 --> 00:25:16,170
chronic form is
constrictive pericarditis. A

487
00:25:16,170 --> 00:25:19,390
thick fibrocalcific scar
encases the heart, limiting

488
00:25:19,390 --> 00:25:22,090
its ability to fill
properly during diastole.

489
00:25:22,330 --> 00:25:25,790
This also results in a
decrease in cardiac output

490
00:25:25,790 --> 00:25:28,810
since the preload and
stroke volume are decreased.

491
00:25:29,070 --> 00:25:32,110
This mimics restrictive
cardiomyopathy.

492
00:25:32,110 --> 00:25:34,910
The scar can get so
big that it can be 1

493
00:25:34,910 --> 00:25:37,840
cm in thickness, which
is termed concretiocordus

494
00:25:38,130 --> 00:25:40,650
since it resembles
a plaster mold.

495
00:25:41,130 --> 00:25:44,510
Neither hypertrophy or
dilation of the heart can occur

496
00:25:44,510 --> 00:25:48,350
since the scar is so
noncompliant and dense so that

497
00:25:48,350 --> 00:25:50,550
the heart cannot adapt to
the demands of the body.

498
00:25:50,610 --> 00:25:53,530
The main causes of
constrictive pericarditis

499
00:25:53,530 --> 00:25:56,610
are idiopathic in
nature, heart surgery,

500
00:25:56,770 --> 00:25:58,710
radiation of the chest,

501
00:25:58,870 --> 00:26:00,910
or tuberculosis.

502
00:26:04,030 --> 00:26:06,630
Shifting gears, we will
now discuss our final

503
00:26:06,630 --> 00:26:10,030
topic, which is cardiac
tumors. Luckily,

504
00:26:10,150 --> 00:26:12,510
the primary cardiac
tumors are rare and mostly

505
00:26:12,510 --> 00:26:15,710
benign. It is far more likely
that tumors found in the

506
00:26:15,710 --> 00:26:18,390
heart are metastases from
elsewhere in the body.

507
00:26:18,650 --> 00:26:20,070
Although rare,

508
00:26:20,390 --> 00:26:22,810
myxomas are the most
common primary cardiac

509
00:26:22,810 --> 00:26:26,030
tumor, followed by
fibromas, lipomas,

510
00:26:26,310 --> 00:26:30,210
papillary fibroelastomas,
and rhabdomyomas.

511
00:26:31,010 --> 00:26:33,950
Sarcomas are the malignant
primary cardiac tumors,

512
00:26:33,950 --> 00:26:36,770
of which angiosarcomas
are the most common.

513
00:26:37,510 --> 00:26:39,770
Symptoms of the
benign primary cardiac

514
00:26:39,770 --> 00:26:41,950
tumors are typically
characteristic of where

515
00:26:41,950 --> 00:26:44,230
they are located in
the heart and can arise

516
00:26:44,230 --> 00:26:47,230
from obstruction,
thromboembolic events,

517
00:26:47,390 --> 00:26:49,750
conduction defects,
and blockage

518
00:26:49,750 --> 00:26:51,210
of the coronary arteries.

519
00:26:51,450 --> 00:26:53,330
It is also important
to note, if a

520
00:26:53,330 --> 00:26:55,150
tumor is located in
the left, you may

521
00:26:55,150 --> 00:26:57,170
see symptoms of
left heart failure,

522
00:26:57,200 --> 00:26:59,150
and if they are on
the right side, you

523
00:26:59,150 --> 00:27:01,650
may see symptoms of
right heart failure.

524
00:27:04,700 --> 00:27:07,110
Starting off with
myxomas, again, they

525
00:27:07,110 --> 00:27:09,350
are the most common
primary cardiac tumor.

526
00:27:09,390 --> 00:27:12,410
These tumors are associated
with germline mutations

527
00:27:12,410 --> 00:27:15,450
of an alpha regulatory
subunit on cyclic AMP

528
00:27:15,450 --> 00:27:21,140
-dependent protein kinase
type 1, also called PRKAR1A.

529
00:27:21,670 --> 00:27:24,470
This enzyme is a
tumor suppressor gene.

530
00:27:25,230 --> 00:27:27,830
Individuals with this
mutation develop what is known

531
00:27:27,830 --> 00:27:31,290
as CARNI complex, which
is an autosomal dominant

532
00:27:31,290 --> 00:27:34,490
condition comprising of
myxomas of the heart and skin,

533
00:27:34,970 --> 00:27:36,610
hyperpigmentation of the skin,

534
00:27:36,610 --> 00:27:38,310
and endocrine overactivity.

535
00:27:38,410 --> 00:27:41,690
These tumors are thought
to arise from multipotent

536
00:27:41,690 --> 00:27:44,450
mesenchymal stem cells
since the cells have

537
00:27:44,450 --> 00:27:46,930
characteristics of
primitive cardiac myocytes

538
00:27:46,930 --> 00:27:50,750
and endothelial cell
precursors. It is important

539
00:27:50,750 --> 00:27:52,910
to know where the
different benign primary

540
00:27:52,910 --> 00:27:56,050
cardiac tumors are typically
found. In this case,

541
00:27:56,050 --> 00:27:58,470
myxomas are usually
found in the left atrium.

542
00:27:58,690 --> 00:28:01,010
An example of this is
seen in the picture.

543
00:28:01,350 --> 00:28:03,830
Just based on the size,
you would imagine that that

544
00:28:03,830 --> 00:28:06,350
myxoma may have led to
symptoms of obstruction.

545
00:28:06,930 --> 00:28:10,290
Histology of this tumor
shows stellated, fusiform,

546
00:28:10,290 --> 00:28:13,810
and polygonal cells in an
amorphous myxoid matrix.

547
00:28:17,490 --> 00:28:20,810
Here is another picture of
a myxoma located in the left

548
00:28:20,810 --> 00:28:23,690
atrium of the heart and
the slated fusiform cells

549
00:28:23,690 --> 00:28:26,990
and polygonal cells in the
myxoid matrix on the right.

550
00:28:30,430 --> 00:28:33,070
The second most
common primary benign

551
00:28:33,070 --> 00:28:35,430
cardiac tumor is
the cardiac fibroma.

552
00:28:35,490 --> 00:28:38,130
As the name suggests,
it is composed

553
00:28:38,130 --> 00:28:40,210
of connective tissue
and fibroblasts.

554
00:28:40,750 --> 00:28:42,910
This cardiac tumor is
mostly found in the

555
00:28:42,910 --> 00:28:45,390
left ventricle, and
just like myxomas,

556
00:28:45,390 --> 00:28:47,410
the symptoms arise
from the same things.

557
00:28:47,610 --> 00:28:50,470
Obstruction, coronary
artery compromise,

558
00:28:50,750 --> 00:28:53,830
thromboembolic events,
and conduction defects.

559
00:28:54,110 --> 00:28:56,790
This one is also
associated with a syndrome

560
00:28:56,790 --> 00:28:59,290
called nevoid basal
cell carcinoma

561
00:28:59,290 --> 00:29:01,990
syndrome, also known
as Gorlin syndrome.

562
00:29:02,350 --> 00:29:05,270
People develop basal
cell carcinomas,

563
00:29:05,430 --> 00:29:07,990
odontogenic keratocysts,
which are located

564
00:29:07,990 --> 00:29:12,390
in the jaw, and 2 to
20% of individuals

565
00:29:12,390 --> 00:29:15,010
with this condition
get cardiac fibromas.

566
00:29:15,190 --> 00:29:17,450
This all occurs from a mutation

567
00:29:17,450 --> 00:29:20,290
in PTCH1 tumor suppressor gene.

568
00:29:20,450 --> 00:29:22,550
This picture on the
right highlights the

569
00:29:22,550 --> 00:29:24,610
location of the left
ventricle as well as the

570
00:29:24,610 --> 00:29:27,370
histology of connective
tissue and fibroblasts.

571
00:29:30,630 --> 00:29:33,150
Lipomas are usually seen
in the skin, but they

572
00:29:33,150 --> 00:29:35,710
can occur elsewhere in
the body, even the heart.

573
00:29:35,910 --> 00:29:38,490
Just like those that occur
in the skin, they are

574
00:29:38,490 --> 00:29:41,730
composed of mature adipocytes
and tend to form in

575
00:29:41,730 --> 00:29:43,890
the left ventricle or
right atrium of the heart.

576
00:29:44,270 --> 00:29:47,210
People with cardiac lipomas
might not even know that

577
00:29:47,210 --> 00:29:49,570
they have one, but just like
the previously mentioned

578
00:29:49,570 --> 00:29:52,750
primary tumors, if they get
big enough, they can obstruct

579
00:29:52,750 --> 00:29:55,170
blood flow within the
heart, leading to symptoms.

580
00:29:55,530 --> 00:29:57,630
There have even been
cases of cardiac

581
00:29:57,630 --> 00:29:59,810
lipomas that compressed
the superior vena

582
00:29:59,810 --> 00:30:02,250
cava when they involved
the right atrium.

583
00:30:02,250 --> 00:30:05,070
The picture on the lower
right shows a fairly

584
00:30:05,070 --> 00:30:08,030
big cardiac lipoma
that was removed, most

585
00:30:08,030 --> 00:30:10,230
likely from severe
symptoms of obstruction.

586
00:30:13,290 --> 00:30:16,070
The primary benign
cardiac tumor that you

587
00:30:16,070 --> 00:30:18,530
will find on valves
are fibroelastomas.

588
00:30:18,790 --> 00:30:21,090
The exact pathogenesis of these

589
00:30:21,090 --> 00:30:22,950
tumors is not quite understood.

590
00:30:23,190 --> 00:30:25,870
However, it is believed that
they are hamartomas, which

591
00:30:25,870 --> 00:30:28,090
are abnormal growths made
up of the same tissue

592
00:30:28,090 --> 00:30:30,950
from which it grows, which
is why it is composed of

593
00:30:30,950 --> 00:30:34,070
collagen and surrounded by a
layer of endothelial cells,

594
00:30:34,210 --> 00:30:36,250
just like the cardiac valves.

595
00:30:36,330 --> 00:30:39,010
However, there is another
theory that these lesions

596
00:30:39,010 --> 00:30:41,950
are acquired and begin
as microthrombi that join

597
00:30:41,950 --> 00:30:45,170
its sites of minor
endothelial damage on valvular

598
00:30:45,170 --> 00:30:48,510
surfaces that evolve into
these types of tumors.

599
00:30:49,390 --> 00:30:52,030
embolization is often
a primary concern with

600
00:30:52,030 --> 00:30:54,410
this cardiac tumor
and can lead to stroke

601
00:30:54,410 --> 00:30:57,430
or myocardial infarction
if they occlude

602
00:30:57,430 --> 00:31:01,050
coronary artery orifices
and may lead to death.

603
00:31:01,490 --> 00:31:04,650
Due to the risk of stroke
and MI, from the left side

604
00:31:04,650 --> 00:31:07,510
of papillary fibroelastomas,
they tend to be removed

605
00:31:07,510 --> 00:31:10,510
with surgery. The decision
to remove the right side of

606
00:31:10,510 --> 00:31:13,690
ones is a more difficult
decision that pros and cons.

607
00:31:17,290 --> 00:31:19,970
Fibroelastomas are classically
described as having an

608
00:31:19,970 --> 00:31:22,210
appearance of a sea anemone
as you can see in the

609
00:31:22,210 --> 00:31:25,450
picture the left. They have
a central stalk and a frond

610
00:31:25,450 --> 00:31:29,690
like arms projecting outwards.
On histology you'll see

611
00:31:29,690 --> 00:31:32,850
primarily collagen with an
outer layer of endothelium.

612
00:31:36,050 --> 00:31:39,530
The last major benign
primary cardiac tumor we will

613
00:31:39,530 --> 00:31:43,470
talk about is the rhabdomyoma.
This one is the most

614
00:31:43,470 --> 00:31:46,770
common primary cardiac
tumor in childhood. It is

615
00:31:46,770 --> 00:31:49,030
important to know that this
tumor is associated with

616
00:31:49,030 --> 00:31:53,950
tuberous sclerosis from
mutations in TSC1 and TSC2.

617
00:31:54,090 --> 00:31:56,810
Other findings in
individuals with tuberous

618
00:31:56,810 --> 00:32:00,650
sclerosis are ash leaf
spots, chagrin patches,

619
00:32:00,770 --> 00:32:03,470
cortical tumors in
the brain, giant cell

620
00:32:03,470 --> 00:32:07,050
astrocytomas, and
renal angiomyolipomas.

621
00:32:07,510 --> 00:32:10,670
Cardiac rhabdomyomas
are commonly not found

622
00:32:10,670 --> 00:32:14,010
as a solitary mass and
are typically found to

623
00:32:14,010 --> 00:32:17,370
involve ventricles and
sometimes the atria.

624
00:32:17,770 --> 00:32:20,770
The characteristic
finding on histology is

625
00:32:20,770 --> 00:32:22,850
the spider cell, which
has a small central

626
00:32:22,850 --> 00:32:26,330
nuclei and abundant glycogen
-rich clear cytoplasm

627
00:32:26,330 --> 00:32:28,810
with fibrillar
processes containing

628
00:32:28,810 --> 00:32:30,910
sarcomeres that radiate
to the edge of the cell.

629
00:32:30,910 --> 00:32:33,290
With their location
within the heart muscle,

630
00:32:33,290 --> 00:32:35,350
they can present with
arrhythmias and heart

631
00:32:35,350 --> 00:32:38,470
failure, although most
are as asymptomatic.

632
00:32:38,730 --> 00:32:41,090
It is important to
note that these tumors

633
00:32:41,090 --> 00:32:43,810
can spontaneously
regress over time.

634
00:32:46,990 --> 00:32:49,850
On the left is the spider
cell with the fibrillar

635
00:32:49,850 --> 00:32:52,930
processes that radiate to the
margins, and on the right,

636
00:32:52,930 --> 00:32:56,010
you'll see multiple rhabdomyomas
in the heart muscle.

637
00:32:59,750 --> 00:33:03,250
here are some very rare
benign primary cardiac tumors

638
00:33:03,250 --> 00:33:06,630
that are interesting the
first is the cystic tumor the

639
00:33:06,630 --> 00:33:09,530
AV node which as the name
suggests is found in the AV

640
00:33:09,530 --> 00:33:12,930
nodal region with its
involvement in the cardiac

641
00:33:12,930 --> 00:33:16,150
conduction system this tumor
can result in sudden death

642
00:33:16,150 --> 00:33:19,650
there are also hemangiomas
which are highly vascular

643
00:33:19,650 --> 00:33:24,030
tumors neurofibromas have
plexiform and scattered spindle

644
00:33:24,030 --> 00:33:27,530
cells and teratomas which
have all germinal layers

645
00:33:27,530 --> 00:33:30,970
present and are found in
the young a very interesting

646
00:33:30,970 --> 00:33:34,470
tumor of the heart is the
lyomyoma which can be primary

647
00:33:34,470 --> 00:33:37,390
but there are some that
hypothesize that cardiac

648
00:33:37,390 --> 00:33:41,150
lyomyomas are actually
metastases from lyomyomas of the

649
00:33:41,150 --> 00:33:45,000
uterus that travel through
the inferior vena cava lastly

650
00:33:45,390 --> 00:33:49,970
are also lymphangiomas that
have that contain vascular

651
00:33:49,970 --> 00:33:53,970
malformations with lymphatic
elements just to emphasize

652
00:33:53,970 --> 00:34:00,750
these tumors are extremely
rare here we have malignant

653
00:34:00,750 --> 00:34:03,570
primary cardiac tumors
since these cancers are

654
00:34:03,570 --> 00:34:06,010
derived from supportive and
connective tissues they are

655
00:34:06,010 --> 00:34:10,070
classified as sarcomas the
sarcoma is named depending

656
00:34:10,070 --> 00:34:13,100
on what tissue type is growing
malignantly angiosarcomas

657
00:34:13,890 --> 00:34:16,590
are the most common malignant
primary cardiac tumor

658
00:34:16,590 --> 00:34:18,950
and are usually found on
the right side of the heart.

659
00:34:19,490 --> 00:34:21,850
Angio implies
that the cancer is

660
00:34:21,850 --> 00:34:23,530
formed from blood
or lymph vessels.

661
00:34:23,670 --> 00:34:26,210
To emphasize how
rare that these are,

662
00:34:26,330 --> 00:34:29,450
there were only around
100,000 primary cardiac

663
00:34:29,450 --> 00:34:32,790
tumors reported in the
span of 12 years, of which

664
00:34:32,790 --> 00:34:36,070
only 0.8% were malignant,
according to one study.

665
00:34:39,730 --> 00:34:42,030
Finally, we have
metastatic tumors.

666
00:34:42,130 --> 00:34:44,330
These are much more
likely to be found in

667
00:34:44,330 --> 00:34:46,270
the heart than primary
cardiac tumors.

668
00:34:46,590 --> 00:34:49,970
Lung, breast, and GI
carcinomas may spread to

669
00:34:49,970 --> 00:34:52,930
the heart as well as
lymphomas and leukemias.

670
00:34:53,050 --> 00:34:55,450
The cancer that is most
likely to spread to the

671
00:34:55,450 --> 00:34:58,070
heart is malignant
melanoma as you can see in

672
00:34:58,070 --> 00:35:00,090
the picture of the heart
on the lower right.

673
00:35:00,410 --> 00:35:02,210
Notice the extent and number of

674
00:35:02,210 --> 00:35:03,990
the metastases
within that heart.

675
00:35:04,810 --> 00:35:07,290
When metastases invade
the heart tissue it

676
00:35:07,290 --> 00:35:09,270
leads to fibrosis
and stiffening of the

677
00:35:09,270 --> 00:35:12,210
muscle leading to
restrictive cardiomyopathy.

678
00:35:12,410 --> 00:35:15,230
As with any cancer that
grows within the myocardium,

679
00:35:15,230 --> 00:35:17,400
it can interfere with
the conduction system,

680
00:35:17,400 --> 00:35:20,510
leading to heart blocks
or bundle branch blocks.

681
00:35:23,950 --> 00:35:27,190
Here is the summary slide.
I just want to emphasize

682
00:35:27,190 --> 00:35:29,610
that myocarditis is
caused by many different

683
00:35:29,610 --> 00:35:32,470
infectious and non-infectious
causes, and that it

684
00:35:32,470 --> 00:35:35,210
may lead to dilated
cardiomyopathy or restrictive

685
00:35:35,210 --> 00:35:38,670
if it is the chronic active
form. It is important

686
00:35:38,670 --> 00:35:41,430
to note that the EMB is
the gold standard for

687
00:35:41,430 --> 00:35:44,790
diagnosis. However, it is
very rarely used if getting

688
00:35:44,790 --> 00:35:47,030
one does not alter how
the patient is treated.

689
00:35:47,730 --> 00:35:50,570
Pericardial disease
involves the pericardium and

690
00:35:50,570 --> 00:35:53,390
the pericardial space.
There is inflammation with

691
00:35:53,390 --> 00:35:57,170
or without pericardial
effusion. It may be acute or

692
00:35:57,170 --> 00:36:00,270
chronic and most involve
some level of fibrosis.

693
00:36:00,790 --> 00:36:03,670
Lastly, it is important
to know primary cardiac

694
00:36:03,670 --> 00:36:06,570
tumors are rare with the
majority being benign.

695
00:36:06,570 --> 00:36:09,350
They could be asymptomatic
but may lead to obstruction

696
00:36:09,350 --> 00:36:12,590
or conduction issues.
Please familiarize

697
00:36:12,590 --> 00:36:15,190
yourself with the most
common locations for each.

698
00:36:17,870 --> 00:36:20,590
Thank you so much for
your attention. Here

699
00:36:20,590 --> 00:36:22,710
is the lecture feedback
form. Please don't

700
00:36:22,710 --> 00:36:24,770
hesitate to email me
with any questions that

701
00:36:24,770 --> 00:36:26,870
you have on the subject.
Good luck to you

702
00:36:26,870 --> 00:36:28,950
all in your studies and
your future careers.